{"type":"message","id":"303735be","parentId":"76f3d0df","timestamp":"2026-05-12T21:21:11.718Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_cWXDs1Ww4vzr58lNDLiRdZev","toolName":"memory_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/research/maxi-instructions.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1,\n      \"endLine\": 17,\n      \"score\": 0.5145012199878692,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.7350017428398132,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"# Instructions for Maxi — Research Cron Jobs\\n\\n## What to Say to Maxi (Copy-Paste Ready)\\n\\n---\\n\\n@Maxi — I need you to take over research cron jobs for me. Here are the 9 research tasks:\\n\\n**Daily (4 jobs):**\\n• **AI Landscape Brief** — 1 PM daily. Search for: new AI model releases, benchmark changes, API/pricing updates. Post a 3-bullet summary to this channel. Save the full summary to `memory/research/YYYY-MM-DD-ai-landscape.md`\\n• **Local LLM & Edge AI** — 3 PM daily. Search for: new small models (1B-8B), quantization methods, Ollama/llama.cpp updates, CPU inference improvements. Post 3 bullets. Save to `memory/research/YYYY-MM-DD-local-llm.md`\\n• **Security Pulse** — 5 PM daily. Search for: CVE\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-04-20.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 26,\n      \"endLine\": 55,\n      \"score\": 0.47452273070812223,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6778896152973175,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- First test job produced `memory/research/2026-04-19_local-llm.md` (correct date)\\n\\n### GitHub Integration — ACTIVE ✅\\n- Repo created: `github.com/kennethbrendangaffney-byte/openclaw-workspace`\\n- Git configured with user identity and `gh auth git-credential`\\n- Auto-backup cron job recreates git commit/push on schedule\\n- STANDING_ORDERS.md pushed to GitHub\\n\\n### STANDING_ORDERS.md Created 📝\\n- Daily operating manual for autonomous morning routine\\n- Covers: morning checks, daily tasks, research management, GitHub protocol, communication style, boundaries (red/yellow/green), emergency procedures\\n- Ken's instruction: \\\"You wake up, check the orders, do the routine.\\\"\\n\\n### Qwen3.6 & Gemma 4 Research \",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-04-20.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 46,\n      \"endLine\": 63,\n      \"score\": 0.4686188906431198,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6694555580615997,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- Successfully authenticated via browser flow (`ollama signin`)\\n- Web search and fetch tools now working\\n- Models available: qwen2.5:7b (4.7GB), qwen2.5:3b, nomic-embed-text\\n\\n### System Health\\n- 15GB RAM available, low load, 23h uptime\\n- OpenClaw version: 2026.4.14 (2026.4.15 update available)\\n- 7 research files produced by April 19-20 cron jobs\\n\\n### Key Decisions\\n- **Model stack**: BitNet 2B for fast local interactive; qwen2.5:7b as backup; kimi k2p5 for cloud research cron jobs\\n- **Remote access**: Sunshine + Moonlight + Tailscale (no port forwarding)\\n- **Date handling**: Explicit \\\"Current date: 2026\\\" in cron prompts to prevent subagent confusion\\n- **Autonomy**: STANDING_ORDERS.md enables \",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/research/2026-05-10_ai-tools.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1,\n      \"endLine\": 30,\n      \"score\": 0.45268912017345425,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6466987431049347,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"# AI Tools Research Summary — May 10, 2026\\n\\n> Research focus: Practical AI tools for productivity, development, creative work, and local/self-hosted options.  \\n> Sources: Web search + article extraction.  \\n> Compiled by: Karen (cron job `research-ai-tools`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Table of Contents\\n\\n1. [Frontier Models (Q2 2026)](#1-frontier-models-q2-2026)\\n2. [Coding & Development Tools](#2-coding--development-tools)\\n3. [Local / Self-Hosted AI](#3-local--self-hosted-ai)\\n4. [Productivity & Workflow](#4-productivity--workflow)\\n5. [Creative Tools (Image, Video, Audio)](#5-creative-tools-image-video-audio)\\n6. [AI Agents & Automation](#6-ai-agents--automation)\\n7. [Notable Releases This Quarter](#7-notable-rele\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-01.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 84,\n      \"endLine\": 97,\n      \"score\": 0.4498312026262283,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6426160037517548,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"Paperclip is well-designed for **managing multiple AI agents as a team**. Right now you have Karen (local) + KC (cloud). That's two agents. Cron handles two agents fine. Paperclip's value multiplies when you have 5+ agents with handoffs, budgets, and approval workflows.\\n\\nYour cron system is simple, reliable, and doesn't need replacing yet. Paperclip is worth watching, not worth migrating to today.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Exploration by Karen + KC, 2026-05-01*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Evening Log — 2026-05-01\\n\\nToday was a solid deep-dive day. Ken spent the afternoon with KC and me exploring Paperclip — evaluating whether it could replace or augment the current cron automation setup. We mapped out what it offers (dashboard, m\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/research/2026-04-19_karen-self-research.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 489,\n      \"endLine\": 527,\n      \"score\": 0.44801588654518126,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6400226950645447,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- [ ] Evaluate memory-wiki plugin for knowledge management\\n- [ ] Consider multi-agent setup if workflow isolation needed\\n- [ ] Create custom skills for Ken's recurring workflows\\n\\n### Ongoing\\n\\n- [ ] Weekly review of MEMORY.md distillation from daily notes\\n- [ ] Monthly review of cron job 