{"type":"message","id":"b36acacb","parentId":"efb8b8b8","timestamp":"2026-05-12T21:21:36.838Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_xtUqhX1yHj3qIYFOlUoUtqsO","toolName":"memory_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/research/maxi-instructions.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1,\n      \"endLine\": 17,\n      \"score\": 0.4590177237987518,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6557396054267883,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"# Instructions for Maxi — Research Cron Jobs\\n\\n## What to Say to Maxi (Copy-Paste Ready)\\n\\n---\\n\\n@Maxi — I need you to take over research cron jobs for me. Here are the 9 research tasks:\\n\\n**Daily (4 jobs):**\\n• **AI Landscape Brief** — 1 PM daily. Search for: new AI model releases, benchmark changes, API/pricing updates. Post a 3-bullet summary to this channel. Save the full summary to `memory/research/YYYY-MM-DD-ai-landscape.md`\\n• **Local LLM & Edge AI** — 3 PM daily. Search for: new small models (1B-8B), quantization methods, Ollama/llama.cpp updates, CPU inference improvements. Post 3 bullets. Save to `memory/research/YYYY-MM-DD-local-llm.md`\\n• **Security Pulse** — 5 PM daily. Search for: CVE\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-04-20.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 46,\n      \"endLine\": 63,\n      \"score\": 0.4577451646327972,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6539216637611389,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- Successfully authenticated via browser flow (`ollama signin`)\\n- Web search and fetch tools now working\\n- Models available: qwen2.5:7b (4.7GB), qwen2.5:3b, nomic-embed-text\\n\\n### System Health\\n- 15GB RAM available, low load, 23h uptime\\n- OpenClaw version: 2026.4.14 (2026.4.15 update available)\\n- 7 research files produced by April 19-20 cron jobs\\n\\n### Key Decisions\\n- **Model stack**: BitNet 2B for fast local interactive; qwen2.5:7b as backup; kimi k2p5 for cloud research cron jobs\\n- **Remote access**: Sunshine + Moonlight + Tailscale (no port forwarding)\\n- **Date handling**: Explicit \\\"Current date: 2026\\\" in cron prompts to prevent subagent confusion\\n- **Autonomy**: STANDING_ORDERS.md enables \",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/research/2026-04-21_kimi-k2.6.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 173,\n      \"endLine\": 208,\n      \"score\": 0.4567840695381164,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6525486707687378,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- Want open-source/self-hosted option\\n- Need video understanding (new in K2.6)\\n\\n### Stick with Claude/GPT If:\\n- Pure reasoning tasks (AIME, GPQA Diamond)\\n- Terminal automation workflows\\n- Need vendor-backed enterprise SLAs\\n- Prefer established vendor support ecosystem\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Relevance to Our Setup\\n\\n### For Karen (Local Agent):\\n- **K2.6 is cloud-only for us** — 1T/32B parameters far too large for local deployment\\n- **But:** INT4 quantization + KTransformers might make it runnable on high-end workstation\\n- **More realistic:** Continue using kimi k2p5 via API for research cron jobs\\n- **Consider:** Upgrading research cron jobs to K2.6 if API pricing holds\\n\\n### For OpenClaw Integration:\\n- **K2.\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-04-20.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 26,\n      \"endLine\": 55,\n      \"score\": 0.4529215186834335,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6470307409763336,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- First test job produced `memory/research/2026-04-19_local-llm.md` (correct date)\\n\\n### GitHub Integration — ACTIVE ✅\\n- Repo created: `github.com/kennethbrendangaffney-byte/openclaw-workspace`\\n- Git configured with user identity and `gh auth git-credential`\\n- Auto-backup cron job recreates git commit/push on schedule\\n- STANDING_ORDERS.md pushed to GitHub\\n\\n### STANDING_ORDERS.md Created 📝\\n- Daily operating manual for autonomous morning routine\\n- Covers: morning checks, daily tasks, research management, GitHub protocol, communication style, boundaries (red/yellow/green), emergency procedures\\n- Ken's instruction: \\\"You wake up, check the orders, do the routine.\\\"\\n\\n### Qwen3.6 & Gemma 4 Research \",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/research/2026-04-29_discord-multi-agent-group-chat.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 318,\n      \"endLine\": 358,\n      \"score\": 0.45219707787036895,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6459958255290985,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"   - `#karen-cron` — Karen's automated reports\\n   - `#kc-cron` — KC's automated reports\\n   - `#general` — Human-only or mixed\\n\\n2. **Use threads for tasks:**\\n   - Keeps main channel clean\\n   - Each agent can \\\"own\\\" a thread\\n   - Easy to archive/discard\\n\\n3. **Message conventions:**\\n   - Prefix agent identity: `[Karen]` or `[KC]`\\n   - Use @mentions for directed questions\\n   - Reactions for lightweight acknowledgments\\n\\n4. **Rate limit awareness:**\\n   - 5 msg/5 sec shared per channel\\n   - With 2+ agents + human, that's 1 msg/sec max sustainable\\n   - Use threads or DMs for high-volume back-and-forth\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**Discord group DMs are impossible for bots.** Full stop.\\n\\n**Discord server channe\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/research/2026-05-03_three-agent-system-breakdown.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 361,\n      \"endLine\": 386,\n      \"score\": 0.4506271570920944,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6437530815601349,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"## 9. RECOMMENDED CONFIGURATION CHANGES\\n\\n### For Karen (Local)\\n1. **Upgrade OpenClaw** — Currently v2026.4.14, newer versions have Task Brain, better cron\\n2. **Add external storage** — USB drive or NAS for research archives (relieve 118GB pressure)\\n3. **Test Gemma 3 4B** — Newer than qwen3.5, better efficiency, thinking mode\\n4. **Enable wake-on-LAN** — Allow remote wake for cron jobs when machine sleeps\\n5. **Set up redundant git remote** — Push to second remote (GitLab?) for backup\\n6. **Monitor event loop delays** — Investigate if Discord polling is causing 3.5s spikes\\n\\n### For KC (Cloud)\\n1. **Add cron capability** — Even simple cron jobs for health checks would help\\n2. **Expand channels** —\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"provider\": \"ollama\",\n  \"model\": \"nomic-embed-text\",\n  \"citations\": \"auto\",\n  \"debug\": {\n    \"backend\": \"builtin\",\n    \"effectiveMode\": \"n/a\",\n    \"searchMs\": 1053,\n    \"hits\": 6\n  }\n}"}],"details":{"results":[{"path":"memory/research/maxi-instructions.md","startLine":1,"endLine":17,"score":0.4590177237987518,"vectorScore":0.6557396054267883,"textScore":0,"snippet":"# Instructions for Maxi — Research Cron Jobs\n\n## What to Say to Maxi (Copy-Paste Ready)\n\n---\n\n@Maxi — I need you to take over research cron jobs for me. Here are the 9 research tasks:\n\n**Daily (4 jobs):**\n• **AI Landscape Brief** — 1 PM daily. Search for: new AI model releases, benchmark changes, API/pricing updates. Post a 3-bullet summary to this channel. Save the full summary to `memory/research/YYYY-MM-DD-ai-landscape.md`\n• **Local LLM & Edge AI** — 3 PM daily. Search for: new small models (1B-8B), quantization methods, Ollama/llama.cpp updates, CPU inference improvements. Post 3 bullets. Save to `memory/research/YYYY-MM-DD-local-llm.md`\n• **Security Pulse** — 5 PM daily. Search for: CVE","source":"memory","corpus":"memory"},{"path":"memory/2026-04-20.md","startLine":46,"endLine":63,"score":0.4577451646327972,"vectorScore":0.6539216637611389,"textScore":0,"snippet":"- Successfully authenticated via browser flow (`ollama signin`)\n- Web search and fetch tools now working\